
SQL Learning Journal: CDC Adult Vaccination Survey Analysis
Portfolio project: Infectious Disease Data Analysis
Learning stage: Days 1–3 — SQL foundations, filtering, comparisons, and grouped counts
Environment: DB Browser for SQLite (macOS)
Dataset: CDC adult respiratory vaccination survey data, 2024–2025 season (described in the learning conversation as the CDC National Immunization Survey Adult COVID Module / RespVaxView archive)
SQLite table: vax
Status: Learning journal / exploratory analysis. Findings reported from the prior practice conversation are not independently reproduced in this document; rerun the queries against the original dataset before presenting them as verified results.

Project purpose
I am developing practical SQL and public health data analysis skills by exploring adult respiratory vaccination survey data. I am using SQLite to ask reproducible questions about vaccination estimates by race/ethnicity, sex, geography, age, and perceptions of healthcare equity. I am also practicing how to interpret confidence intervals, sample sizes, and the limitations of survey data.

Guiding question: How do estimated 2024–2025 COVID-19 vaccination percentages vary across adult populations and places?

