What I learned and what I will do next
SQL is not only about returning rows: the filters must make the research question valid. A query can run successfully and still compare unrelated indicators.
Labels, spaces, date strings, and column types matter when working with real public health datasets.
Reporting an estimate responsibly means examining confidence intervals, sample sizes, suppression, and geographic definitions.
